 "notes": "Four old kinds kept. Archetypes from saxophone.org museum model pages and Wikipedia; shared lines (Mark VI, Series III, Conn M, Yamaha 62/Custom Z, Keilwerth SX90R) repeat per voice with voice-specific versions only. Dropped: Thomann BariPRO/lowJAZZ (retailer house SKUs, also in r) and the r list; Selmer Supreme tenor folded in as Reference 54 successor version. Left out: Yamaha YAS-62/82Z years (Yamaha, Reverb, Sweetwater blocked 403, so no launch years cited); King Super 20 no tenor detail beyond series I; Conn 'Naked Lady' end year (sources disagree 1962/1968); mouthpieces (Otto Link, Meyer) left to accessories, noted only as a type."
}